# Base integration tests that scripts/check-compat.sh part 2 skips. Ships with no entries (D342).
#
# An entry needs a plan revision that names the test and says what it pins and why the pixel and API
# checks do not protect that. One entry per line, four fields separated by `|`:
#   <path of the test file> | <test name> | <reason> | <D-row>
# The test name is passed to the test binaries as `--skip <name>`, so it skips every test of that
# name in every binary of the run. A line starting with `#` and a blank line are ignored.

crates/lune-ui-core/tests/ui_touch.rs | a_tap_answers_as_a_mouse_click_does_except_the_hover_after_the_lift | pins focus on a touch press; M5 D361 moves a touch press's focus to its tap, long press or drag start for apps that turned touch on (D16); no API or mouse, keyboard or wheel pixel check covers touch focus timing. | D361
crates/lune-ui-core/tests/ui_touch.rs | a_touch_outside_a_popover_dismisses_it_and_a_touch_focuses_a_focusable_widget | pins focus on a touch press; M5 D361 moves a touch press's focus to its tap, long press or drag start for apps that turned touch on (D16); no API or mouse, keyboard or wheel pixel check covers touch focus timing. | D361
apps/gallery/src/catalogue.rs | every_widget_module_is_claimed_by_an_entry | the base gallery's unit test lists every widget module of the tree's lune-ui-core and fails on any module its own catalogue does not claim, so every new widget module (M6's bottom_sheet.rs, gesture_track.rs, ...) breaks it; it pins the base gallery's catalogue bookkeeping, not API, behaviour or pixels, which parts 1 and 3 cover. | D414
